\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TVerbpattern6
\item[* relevant examples:]
\item[subrule 1] El milagro se le ha revelado (a \'{e}l).\\
                 Me gusta el libro; Le doy un libro a Juan. 
\item[subrule 2] Le qued\'{o} claro que .. (vp012)\\
                 Juan me dijo que .. (vp123) \\
                 Me gusta que lo haga (vp012).
\item[subrule 3] Le gusta al chico hacerlo. (vp012)\\
                 Juan le pidi\'{o} a Pedro salir. (vp123)
\item[subrule 4] D\'{\i}me qu\'{e} hago.
\item[subrule 5] Esto me cuesta seis florines.
\item[subrule 6] Juan me parece el m\'{a}s inteligente.
\item[subrule 7] Juan me parece mejor.
\item[subrule 8] Juan me parece contra la propuesta.
\item[subrule 9] Me parece que s\'{\i}.\\
                 Juan me dijo que s\'{\i}.
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] Verbppropformation
\item[* class:] TC: Verbpatternrules
\item[* date of creation:] 22-SEP-1987 15:45:00  
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster
\item[* copied from:] Jan Odijk
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 22/02/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster \\
\item date: 01/11/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster \\
Added VARPREPP.{\em specQ} in TVerbpattern6. \\
Although the value of the attribute is probably irrelevant in this case 
(Indirect Object), it has been added here analogously to other VARPREPP's. 
\item date: 26/07/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster \\
Attribute modo for SENTENCEVAR added.
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] Verbpattern-transformation for {\em two} arguments in the VP,
one of which is an {\em "ANP"}.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] none
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:] dna
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:] doc.nr.108
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
Contrary to Dutch, the IO follows the other argument.\\
If the first argument is a sentence, the order sentence/IO will be reversed 
by extraposition.\\
Only a rule has to be added to extrapose a Prepositional argument.
(SUBRULE 8a). 
\item modifications:\\
Attribute "infsort" added.
\end{enumerate}
\end{description}
